{
    // Newest-only slice of the WHOLE test matrix for `validate:tests:newest`, in a
    // SINGLE tsgo program (not the per-connector split that scripts/validate-tests.sh
    // runs for the full `validate:tests`). It keeps the version set the agent works
    // with day-to-day — every db's `newest/` + `types.negative/` (mirrors the
    // runner's `--run-versions newest`), plus the shared infra (lib, templates,
    // db/general, each db's runners.ts) and src — and drops the older version tiers
    // (oldest/, 8_000_000/, …) and domain/.
    //
    // A single program over the newest set fits in far less RAM than a single
    // whole-matrix program (which peaks past 17 GB in tsgo and OOMs — the reason the
    // full `validate:tests` splits per connector): the older tiers + domain are
    // exactly the bulk that pushes it over, so newest peaks ~6 GB — comfortably in
    // RAM. One invocation, one pass/fail: it's the fast inner typecheck loop. The
    // full `validate:tests` (per-connector split) stays the pre-push / CI gate.
    //
    // The newest set is expressed by INCLUDE, so a newly added version-tier folder
    // is auto-excluded here with no edit.
    "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
    "include": [
        "lib/**/*.ts",
        "templates/**/*.ts",
        "db/general/**/*.ts",
        "db/*/newest/**/*.ts",
        "db/*/types.negative/**/*.ts",
        "db/*/runners.ts",
        "../src/**/*.ts"
    ]
}
